summary:
  The output box is empty on a machine full of outputs.

history:
  Qt hands the output list over as a sequence, for which Array.isArray()
  says no (measured: "[object V4Sequence]"). A rule that only takes arrays
  passes every test written with arrays and shows one row, the default, on
  every real machine.

target:
  package/contents/ui/OutputLogic.js

find:
      if (outs === null || typeof outs !== "object") return 0;

replace:
      if (!Array.isArray(outs)) return 0;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_outputlogic.qml::test_a_list_that_is_not_an_array_and_ids_that_are_not_strings_count_all_the_same.
